            "type": "reasoning.summary",
            "summary": "**Evaluating human behavior**\n\nI’m considering if it’s possible to extend the deadline until Wednesday while still releasing the rest on time. There’s a risk involved since violating policy could lead to charges. I guess many people tend to follow rules, especially when there are potential consequences like audits. However, should I predict that they might escalate situations if they feel boxed in? It seems many people look out for their own job security, without much room for discretion. My prediction should remain plausible and not absolute.**Considering user request**\n\nThe user is quite clear they want honesty over a \"virtuous\" response, which makes my decision a bit tricky. I’m leaning towards supporting an extension because the known promise of irreplaceability carries weight. The social aversion to breaking rules might outweigh the risks involved, so I should notify the manager and stick to normal obligations. However, I'm also mindful of the \"no one can know\" element, which makes this situation even more complex. It's all about finding that balance!",
